-- Singapore Penal Code 1871 - Chapter 9, Offences by or relating to public
-- servants (ss 161-171). Part of the state-public group (Chapters 6-10).
--
-- Source: Penal Code 1871, 2020 Revised Edition, SSO current version as at
-- 09 Sep 2026 (inputs/PC1871.txt). Each section's text is quoted above its rules.
--
-- GENERATED by notes/state-public-gen/build.py from the hand-written ladders in
-- notes/state-public-gen/part_servants.py; edit there and rebuild.
--
-- ss 161-165 are the Code's own gratification offences. In practice most
-- corruption is charged under the Prevention of Corruption Act 1960, which is
-- not in this job's inputs; nothing here reads it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-state-public-common`

§ `Chapter 9 - Offences by or relating to public servants`

§§ `s 161 - Public servant taking a gratification, other than legal remuneration, in respect of an official act`

--   161. Whoever, being or expecting to be a public servant, accepts or obtains,
--   or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain, from any person, for himself or
--   for any other person, any gratification whatever, other than legal
--   remuneration, as a motive or reward for doing or forbearing to do any
--   official act, or for showing or forbearing to show, in the exercise of his
--   official functions, favour or disfavour to any person, or for rendering or
--   attempting to render any service or disservice to any person, with the
--   Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any
--   public servant, as such, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.
--
--   Explanations.-"Expecting to be a public servant". If a person not expecting
--   to be in office obtains a gratification by deceiving others into a belief
--   that he is about to be in office, and that he will then serve them, he may
--   be guilty of cheating, but he is not guilty of the offence defined in this
--   section.
--
--   "Gratification". The word "gratification" is not restricted to pecuniary
--   gratifications, or to gratifications estimable in money.
--
--   "Legal remuneration". The words "legal remuneration" are not restricted to
--   remuneration which a public servant can lawfully demand, but include all
--   remuneration which he is permitted by law to accept.
--
--   "A motive or reward for doing". A person who receives a gratification as a
--   motive for doing what he does not intend to do, or as a reward for doing
--   what he has not done, comes within these words.
--
--   Illustrations
--
--   (a) A, a judge, obtains from Z, a banker, a situation in Z's bank for A's
--   brother, as a reward to A for deciding a cause in favour of Z. A has
--   committed the offence defined in this section.
--
--   (b) A, a public servant, induces Z erroneously to believe that A's influence
--   with another public servant has obtained for Z a contract to do work, and
--   thus induces Z to give A money. A has committed the offence defined in this
--   section.
--
--   (c) A, a public servant, induces Z erroneously to believe that A's influence
--   with the Government has obtained a grant of land for Z, and thus induces Z
--   to give A money, as a reward for his service. A has committed the offence
--   defined in this section.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 161 and its Explanations
DECLARE `Official Gratification Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `expecting to be a public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused expecting to be a public servant? (Explanation: a person NOT expecting to be in office who deceives others into believing they soon will be may be guilty of cheating, but not of this offence.)
    accepts
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused accept it?
    obtains
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obtain it?
    `agrees to accept`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused agree to accept it?
    `attempts to obtain`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt to obtain it?
    `any gratification whatever`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what the accused accepted or obtained (or agreed or attempted to) a gratification? (Explanation: not restricted to money or things estimable in money.)
    `other than legal remuneration`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it something other than legal remuneration? (Explanation: legal remuneration includes all remuneration the public servant is permitted by law to accept, not only what can be lawfully demanded.)
    `as a motive or reward`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a motive or reward? (Explanation: a motive for doing what the accused does not intend to do, or a reward for what the accused has not done, counts.)
    `for doing or forbearing to do any official act`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... for doing or forbearing to do an official act?
    `for showing or forbearing to show, in the exercise of his official functions, favour or disfavour to any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... for showing or forbearing to show favour or disfavour to anyone in the exercise of the accused's official functions?
    `for rendering or attempting to render any service or disservice to any person, with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... for rendering or attempting to render any service or disservice to anyone with the Government, a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or a public servant as such?
    `the giver`
        IS A Person @desc The person from whom the gratification was accepted or obtained, as the charge names them
    `the gratification`
        IS A STRING @desc The gratification, as it is to read in the charge - for example "a sum of $5,000"
    `the official act`
        IS A STRING @desc What it was a motive or reward for, as it is to read in the charge - for example "for deciding a cause in favour of the said Zainal bin Osman"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 161
`punishment prescribed by s 161` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "161"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant (or one expecting to be) takes a gratification other than legal remuneration as a motive or reward for an official act, within section 161 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Official Gratification Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `takes a gratification in respect of an official act` f IF
        "Whoever, being"
    AND (    f's `public servant`
         OR  f's `expecting to be a public servant` )
    AND (    f's accepts
         OR  f's obtains
         OR  f's `agrees to accept`
         OR  f's `attempts to obtain` )
    AND "from any person, for himself or for any other person,"
    AND f's `any gratification whatever`
    AND f's `other than legal remuneration`
    AND f's `as a motive or reward`
    AND (    f's `for doing or forbearing to do any official act`
         OR  f's `for showing or forbearing to show, in the exercise of his official functions, favour or disfavour to any person`
         OR  f's `for rendering or attempting to render any service or disservice to any person, with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 161 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant taking a gratification in respect of an official act)
GIVEN f IS AN `Official Gratification Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 161` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `takes a gratification in respect of an official act` f

@export Frame a charge under section 161 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant taking a gratification, other than legal remuneration, in respect of an official act), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Official Gratification Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 161` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "161" "public servant taking a gratification, other than legal remuneration, in respect of an official act"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 161`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 161` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant, did ", (`joined with` " or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's accepts) "accept"), (`included if` (f's obtains) "obtain"), (`included if` (f's `agrees to accept`) "agree to accept"), (`included if` (f's `attempts to obtain`) "attempt to obtain")))), " from ", `one person` (f's `the giver`), ", a gratification other than legal remuneration, namely ", f's `the gratification`, ", as a motive or reward ", f's `the official act`, `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant` OR f's `expecting to be a public servant`) "being or expecting to be a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's accepts OR f's obtains OR f's `agrees to accept` OR f's `attempts to obtain`) "accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `any gratification whatever`) "any gratification"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `other than legal remuneration`) "other than legal remuneration"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `as a motive or reward`) "as a motive or reward"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `for doing or forbearing to do any official act` OR f's `for showing or forbearing to show, in the exercise of his official functions, favour or disfavour to any person` OR f's `for rendering or attempting to render any service or disservice to any person, with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such`) "for an official act, for favour or disfavour, or for service or disservice with the Government or a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (`takes a gratification in respect of an official act` f) "the elements of section 161 taken together")))

§§ `s 162 - Taking a gratification in order, by corrupt or illegal means, to influence a public servant`

--   162. Whoever accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain,
--   from any person, for himself or for any other person, any gratification
--   whatever, as a motive or reward for inducing, by corrupt or illegal means,
--   any public servant to do or to forbear to do any official act, or in the
--   exercise of the official functions of such public servant to show favour or
--   disfavour to any person, or to render or attempt to render any service or
--   disservice to any person, with the Government, or with any Member of
--   Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such, shall be
--   punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with
--   fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 162, 163, 164
DECLARE `Gratification to Influence Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    accepts
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the taker accept it?
    obtains
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the taker obtain it?
    `agrees to accept`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the taker agree to accept it?
    `attempts to obtain`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the taker attempt to obtain it?
    `any gratification whatever`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what the taker accepted or obtained a gratification (not restricted to money - s 161 Explanation)?
    `as a motive or reward for inducing`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a motive or reward for inducing a public servant to act as below?
    `by corrupt or illegal means`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 162: ... by corrupt or illegal means (s 43)?
    `by the exercise of personal influence`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 163: ... by the exercise of personal influence? (s 163 illustration: an advocate arguing a case, a paid drafter of a memorial, a paid agent laying a petition before Government do not exercise or profess to exercise personal influence.)
    `any public servant to do or to forbear to do any official act`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... a public servant to do or forbear to do an official act?
    `in the exercise of the official functions of such public servant to show favour or disfavour to any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... a public servant to show favour or disfavour to anyone in the exercise of official functions?
    `to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... a public servant to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to anyone with the Government, a Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or a public servant?
    `the accused is the taker`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ss 162, 163: Is the accused the person who accepted or obtained the gratification?
    `being a public servant, in respect of whom the offence is committed`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 164: Is the accused the public servant in respect of whom the s 162 or s 163 offence was committed?
    `abets the offence`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 164: Did the accused abet that offence (s 107 - defined in pc-general-part; joined at integration)?
    `the giver`
        IS A Person @desc The person from whom the gratification was accepted or obtained, as the charge names them
    `the taker`
        IS A Person @desc For s 164: the person who took the gratification, as the charge names them
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant to be influenced, as the charge names them
    `the gratification`
        IS A STRING @desc The gratification, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 162
`punishment prescribed by s 162` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "162"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a gratification is taken as a motive or reward for inducing a public servant by corrupt or illegal means, within section 162 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `takes a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt means` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's accepts
         OR  f's obtains
         OR  f's `agrees to accept`
         OR  f's `attempts to obtain` )
    AND "from any person, for himself or for any other person,"
    AND f's `any gratification whatever`
    AND f's `as a motive or reward for inducing`
    AND f's `by corrupt or illegal means`
    AND (    f's `any public servant to do or to forbear to do any official act`
         OR  f's `in the exercise of the official functions of such public servant to show favour or disfavour to any person`
         OR  f's `to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 162 of the Penal Code 1871 (taking a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt or illegal means)
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 162` f IF
        f's `the accused is the taker`
    AND `takes a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt means` f

@export Frame a charge under section 162 of the Penal Code 1871 (taking a gratification in order, by corrupt or illegal means, to influence a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 162` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "162" "taking a gratification in order, by corrupt or illegal means, to influence a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 162`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 162` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (`joined with` " or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's accepts) "accept"), (`included if` (f's obtains) "obtain"), (`included if` (f's `agrees to accept`) "agree to accept"), (`included if` (f's `attempts to obtain`) "attempt to obtain")))), " from ", `one person` (f's `the giver`), ", a gratification, namely ", f's `the gratification`, ", as a motive or reward for inducing, by corrupt or illegal means, ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, to do or forbear to do an official act or to show favour or disfavour in the exercise of official functions", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is the taker`) "the accused is the person who took the gratification"),
            (`missing unless` (f's accepts OR f's obtains OR f's `agrees to accept` OR f's `attempts to obtain`) "accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `any gratification whatever`) "any gratification"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `as a motive or reward for inducing`) "as a motive or reward for inducing a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `by corrupt or illegal means`) "by corrupt or illegal means"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `any public servant to do or to forbear to do any official act` OR f's `in the exercise of the official functions of such public servant to show favour or disfavour to any person` OR f's `to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such`) "to do or forbear an official act, to show favour or disfavour, or to render service or disservice"),
            (`missing unless` (`takes a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt means` f) "the elements of section 162 taken together")))

§§ `s 163 - Taking a gratification, for the exercise of personal influence with a public servant`

--   163. Whoever accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain,
--   from any person, for himself or for any other person, any gratification
--   whatever, as a motive or reward for inducing, by the exercise of personal
--   influence, any public servant to do or to forbear to do any official act, or
--   in the exercise of the official functions of such public servant to show
--   favour or disfavour to any person, or to render or attempt to render any
--   service or disservice to any person with the Government, or with any Member
--   of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such, shall be
--   punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with
--   fine, or with both.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   An advocate who receives a fee for arguing a case before a judge; a person
--   who receives pay for arranging and correcting a memorial addressed to
--   Government, setting forth the services and claims of the memorialist; a paid
--   agent for a condemned criminal, who lays before the Government statements
--   tending to show that the condemnation was unjust - are not within this
--   section, inasmuch as they do not exercise or profess to exercise personal
--   influence.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 163
`punishment prescribed by s 163` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "163"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a gratification is taken as a motive or reward for inducing a public servant by the exercise of personal influence, within section 163 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `takes a gratification for personal influence with a public servant` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    f's accepts
         OR  f's obtains
         OR  f's `agrees to accept`
         OR  f's `attempts to obtain` )
    AND "from any person, for himself or for any other person,"
    AND f's `any gratification whatever`
    AND f's `as a motive or reward for inducing`
    AND f's `by the exercise of personal influence`
    AND (    f's `any public servant to do or to forbear to do any official act`
         OR  f's `in the exercise of the official functions of such public servant to show favour or disfavour to any person`
         OR  f's `to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 163 of the Penal Code 1871 (taking a gratification for the exercise of personal influence with a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 163` f IF
        f's `the accused is the taker`
    AND `takes a gratification for personal influence with a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 163 of the Penal Code 1871 (taking a gratification for the exercise of personal influence with a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 163` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "163" "taking a gratification for the exercise of personal influence with a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 163`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 163` f)
        (CONCAT "did ", (`joined with` " or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's accepts) "accept"), (`included if` (f's obtains) "obtain"), (`included if` (f's `agrees to accept`) "agree to accept"), (`included if` (f's `attempts to obtain`) "attempt to obtain")))), " from ", `one person` (f's `the giver`), ", a gratification, namely ", f's `the gratification`, ", as a motive or reward for inducing, by the exercise of personal influence, ", `one person` (f's `the public servant`), ", a public servant, to do or forbear to do an official act or to show favour or disfavour in the exercise of official functions", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `the accused is the taker`) "the accused is the person who took the gratification"),
            (`missing unless` (f's accepts OR f's obtains OR f's `agrees to accept` OR f's `attempts to obtain`) "accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `any gratification whatever`) "any gratification"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `as a motive or reward for inducing`) "as a motive or reward for inducing a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `by the exercise of personal influence`) "by the exercise of personal influence"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `any public servant to do or to forbear to do any official act` OR f's `in the exercise of the official functions of such public servant to show favour or disfavour to any person` OR f's `to render or attempt to render any service or disservice to any person with the Government, or with any Member of Parliament or the Cabinet, or with any public servant, as such`) "to do or forbear an official act, to show favour or disfavour, or to render service or disservice"),
            (`missing unless` (`takes a gratification for personal influence with a public servant` f) "the elements of section 163 taken together")))

§§ `s 164 - Punishment for abetment by public servant of the offences above defined`

--   164. Whoever, being a public servant, in respect of whom either of the
--   offences defined in sections 162 and 163 is committed, abets the offence,
--   shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years,
--   or with fine, or with both.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   A is a public servant. B, A's wife, receives a present as a motive for
--   soliciting A to give an office to a particular person. A abets her doing so.
--   B is punishable with imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year, or with
--   fine, or with both. A is punishable with imprisonment for a term which may
--   extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 164
`punishment prescribed by s 164` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "164"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused, the public servant in respect of whom an offence under section 162 or 163 of the Penal Code 1871 is committed, abets it (section 164)
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 164` f IF
        "Whoever,"
    AND f's `being a public servant, in respect of whom the offence is committed`
    AND "either of the offences defined in sections 162 and 163"
    AND (    `takes a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt means` f
         OR  `takes a gratification for personal influence with a public servant` f )
    AND f's `abets the offence`

@export Frame a charge under section 164 of the Penal Code 1871 (abetment by a public servant of an offence under section 162 or 163), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Gratification to Influence Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 164` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "164" "abetment by a public servant of an offence under section 162 or 163"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 164`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 164` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant in respect of whom an offence under section ", (IF `takes a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt means` f THEN "162" ELSE "163"), " of the Penal Code 1871 was committed by ", `one person` (f's `the taker`), ", did abet the said offence", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `being a public servant, in respect of whom the offence is committed`) "being a public servant in respect of whom the offence is committed"),
            (`missing unless` (`takes a gratification to influence a public servant by corrupt means` f OR `takes a gratification for personal influence with a public servant` f) "an offence defined in section 162 or 163"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `abets the offence`) "abets the offence")))

§§ `s 165 - Public servant obtaining any valuable thing, without consideration, from person concerned in any proceeding or business transacted by such public servant`

--   165. Whoever, being a public servant, accepts or obtains, or agrees to
--   accept or attempts to obtain, for himself or for any other person, any
--   valuable thing, without consideration, or for a consideration which he knows
--   to be inadequate, from any person whom he knows to have been, or to be, or
--   to be likely to be concerned in any proceedings or business transacted, or
--   about to be transacted, by such public servant, or having any connection
--   with the official functions of himself or of any public servant to whom he
--   is subordinate, or from any person whom he knows to be interested in or
--   related to the person so concerned, shall be punished with imprisonment for
--   a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both.
--
--   Illustrations
--
--   (a) A, a judge, hires a house of Z, who has a case pending before him. It is
--   agreed that A shall pay $50 a month, the house being such that, if the
--   bargain were made in good faith, A would be required to pay $200 a month. A
--   has obtained a valuable thing from Z without adequate consideration.
--
--   (b) A, a judge, buys of Z, who has a cause pending in A's court, Government
--   promissory notes at a discount, when they are selling in the market at a
--   premium. A has obtained a valuable thing from Z without adequate
--   consideration.
--
--   (c) Z's brother is apprehended and taken before A, a Magistrate, on a charge
--   of perjury. A sells to Z shares in a bank at a premium, when they are
--   selling in the market at a discount. Z pays A for the shares accordingly.
--   The money so obtained by A is a valuable thing obtained by him without
--   adequate consideration.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 165
DECLARE `Valuable Thing Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `the public servant`
        IS A Person @desc The public servant concerned, as the charge names them - for example Sergeant Lim Ah Seng, a police officer attached to Ang Mo Kio Police Division
    accepts
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused accept it?
    obtains
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused obtain it?
    `agrees to accept`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused agree to accept it?
    `attempts to obtain`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused attempt to obtain it?
    `any valuable thing`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a valuable thing (money, shares, a lease on favourable terms ...)?
    `without consideration`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it without consideration?
    `for a consideration which he knows to be inadequate`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it for a consideration the accused knew to be inadequate?
    `from any person whom he knows to have been, or to be, or to be likely to be concerned in any proceedings or business transacted or about to be transacted by such public servant, or having any connection with the official functions of himself or of any public servant to whom he is subordinate`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it from a person the accused knew to have been, to be, or to be likely to be concerned in proceedings or business transacted (or about to be) by the accused, or connected with the official functions of the accused or of a superior?
    `from any person whom he knows to be interested in or related to the person so concerned`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it from a person the accused knew to be interested in, or related to, such a person?
    `the giver`
        IS A Person @desc The person from whom it was obtained, as the charge names them
    `the valuable thing`
        IS A STRING @desc The valuable thing, as it is to read in the charge - for example "the lease of a house at $50 a month"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 165
`punishment prescribed by s 165` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "165"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant obtains a valuable thing without adequate consideration from a person concerned in business the public servant transacts, within section 165 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Valuable Thing Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obtains a valuable thing from a person concerned in his business` f IF
        "Whoever, being a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND (    f's accepts
         OR  f's obtains
         OR  f's `agrees to accept`
         OR  f's `attempts to obtain` )
    AND "for himself or for any other person,"
    AND f's `any valuable thing`
    AND (    f's `without consideration`
         OR  f's `for a consideration which he knows to be inadequate` )
    AND (    f's `from any person whom he knows to have been, or to be, or to be likely to be concerned in any proceedings or business transacted or about to be transacted by such public servant, or having any connection with the official functions of himself or of any public servant to whom he is subordinate`
         OR  f's `from any person whom he knows to be interested in or related to the person so concerned` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 165 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant obtaining a valuable thing without consideration from a person concerned in business transacted by him)
GIVEN f IS A `Valuable Thing Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 165` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `obtains a valuable thing from a person concerned in his business` f

@export Frame a charge under section 165 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant obtaining a valuable thing, without consideration, from a person concerned in business transacted by him), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Valuable Thing Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 165` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "165" "public servant obtaining a valuable thing, without consideration, from a person concerned in business transacted by him"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 165`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 165` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant, did ", (`joined with` " or " (concat (LIST (`included if` (f's accepts) "accept"), (`included if` (f's obtains) "obtain"), (`included if` (f's `agrees to accept`) "agree to accept"), (`included if` (f's `attempts to obtain`) "attempt to obtain")))), " from ", `one person` (f's `the giver`), ", ", f's `the valuable thing`, ", ", (IF f's `without consideration` THEN "without consideration" ELSE "for a consideration which you knew to be inadequate"), ", the said ", f's `the giver`'s name, " being a person whom you knew to be concerned in proceedings or business transacted by you or connected with your official functions", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "being a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's accepts OR f's obtains OR f's `agrees to accept` OR f's `attempts to obtain`) "accepts or obtains, or agrees to accept or attempts to obtain"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `any valuable thing`) "any valuable thing"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `without consideration` OR f's `for a consideration which he knows to be inadequate`) "without consideration, or for a consideration he knows to be inadequate"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `from any person whom he knows to have been, or to be, or to be likely to be concerned in any proceedings or business transacted or about to be transacted by such public servant, or having any connection with the official functions of himself or of any public servant to whom he is subordinate` OR f's `from any person whom he knows to be interested in or related to the person so concerned`) "from a person he knows to be concerned in his proceedings or business, or interested in or related to such a person"),
            (`missing unless` (`obtains a valuable thing from a person concerned in his business` f) "the elements of section 165 taken together")))

§§ `s 166 - Public servant disobeying a direction of the law, with intent to cause injury to any person`

--   166. Whoever, being a public servant, knowingly disobeys any direction of
--   the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public
--   servant, intending to cause, or knowing it to be likely that he will, by
--   such disobedience, cause injury to any person, shall be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with
--   both.
--
--   Illustration
--
--   A, being an officer directed by law to take property under or pursuant to an
--   enforcement order, or in execution in order to satisfy a decree, pronounced
--   in Z's favour by a court of justice, knowingly disobeys that direction of
--   law, with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause injury to Z. A
--   has committed the offence defined in this section.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 166; s 44
DECLARE `Disobeying Direction of Law Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    knowingly
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused act knowingly (s 26D)?
    `disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused disobey a direction of the law as to how the accused was to conduct themselves as a public servant?
    `intending to cause`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend by the disobedience to cause injury to anyone?
    `knowing it to be likely that he will, by such disobedience, cause`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it was likely the disobedience would cause injury to anyone?
    `injury to any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the harm in question an injury (s 44) to a person?
    `the direction`
        IS A STRING @desc The direction of the law, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 166
`punishment prescribed by s 166` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "166"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant knowingly disobeys a direction of the law intending, or knowing it likely, to cause injury, within section 166 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Disobeying Direction of Law Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disobeys a direction of the law with intent to cause injury` f IF
        "Whoever, being a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's knowingly
    AND f's `disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant`
    AND (    f's `intending to cause`
         OR  f's `knowing it to be likely that he will, by such disobedience, cause` )
    AND f's `injury to any person`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 166 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant disobeying a direction of the law with intent to cause injury)
GIVEN f IS A `Disobeying Direction of Law Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 166` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `disobeys a direction of the law with intent to cause injury` f

@export Frame a charge under section 166 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant disobeying a direction of the law, with intent to cause injury), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Disobeying Direction of Law Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 166` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "166" "public servant disobeying a direction of the law, with intent to cause injury"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 166`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 166` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant, did knowingly disobey a direction of the law as to the way in which you were to conduct yourself as such public servant, namely ", f's `the direction`, ", ", (IF f's `intending to cause` THEN "intending" ELSE "knowing it to be likely"), " thereby to cause injury to any person", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "being a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's knowingly) "knowingly"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `disobeys any direction of the law as to the way in which he is to conduct himself as such public servant`) "disobeys a direction of the law as to his conduct as a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending to cause` OR f's `knowing it to be likely that he will, by such disobedience, cause`) "intending, or knowing it to be likely, to cause"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `injury to any person`) "injury to any person")))

§§ `s 167 - Public servant framing an incorrect document or electronic record with intent to cause injury`

--   167. Whoever, being a public servant, and being, as such public servant,
--   charged with the preparation or translation of any document or electronic
--   record, frames or translates that document or electronic record in a manner
--   which he knows or believes to be incorrect, intending thereby to cause, or
--   knowing it to be likely that he may thereby cause, injury to any person,
--   shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years,
--   or with fine, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 167; ss 29, 29B, 44
DECLARE `Incorrect Document Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `charged, as such public servant, with the preparation or translation of any document or electronic record`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the accused, as a public servant, charged with preparing or translating a document (s 29) or electronic record (s 29B)?
    `frames or translates that document or electronic record`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused frame or translate it?
    `in a manner which he knows or believes to be incorrect`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc ... in a manner the accused knew or believed to be incorrect?
    `intending thereby to cause`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend by it to cause injury to anyone?
    `knowing it to be likely that he may thereby cause`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it was likely to cause injury to anyone?
    `injury to any person`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the harm in question an injury (s 44) to a person?
    `the document`
        IS A STRING @desc The document or electronic record, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 167
`punishment prescribed by s 167` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "167"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 36
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether a public servant charged with preparing or translating a document frames it incorrectly with intent, or knowing it likely, to cause injury, within section 167 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS AN `Incorrect Document Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `frames an incorrect document with intent to cause injury` f IF
        "Whoever, being a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `charged, as such public servant, with the preparation or translation of any document or electronic record`
    AND f's `frames or translates that document or electronic record`
    AND f's `in a manner which he knows or believes to be incorrect`
    AND (    f's `intending thereby to cause`
         OR  f's `knowing it to be likely that he may thereby cause` )
    AND f's `injury to any person`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 167 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant framing an incorrect document with intent to cause injury)
GIVEN f IS AN `Incorrect Document Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 167` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `frames an incorrect document with intent to cause injury` f

@export Frame a charge under section 167 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant framing an incorrect document or electronic record with intent to cause injury), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS AN `Incorrect Document Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 167` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "167" "public servant framing an incorrect document or electronic record with intent to cause injury"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 167`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 167` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant charged, as such public servant, with the preparation of ", f's `the document`, ", did frame the same in a manner which you knew or believed to be incorrect, ", (IF f's `intending thereby to cause` THEN "intending" ELSE "knowing it to be likely"), " thereby to cause injury to any person", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "being a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `charged, as such public servant, with the preparation or translation of any document or electronic record`) "charged, as such, with the preparation or translation of the document"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `frames or translates that document or electronic record`) "frames or translates it"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in a manner which he knows or believes to be incorrect`) "in a manner he knows or believes to be incorrect"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `intending thereby to cause` OR f's `knowing it to be likely that he may thereby cause`) "intending, or knowing it to be likely, to cause"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `injury to any person`) "injury to any person")))

§§ `s 168 - Public servant unlawfully engaging in trade`

--   168. Whoever, being a public servant, and being legally bound as such public
--   servant not to engage in trade, engages in trade, shall be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with
--   both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 ss 168, 169
DECLARE `Public Servant Trading Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person concerned a public servant within section 21 of the Penal Code 1871 - for example a police officer, or an officer of the Government or of a statutory body with a duty of maintaining law and order? (Chapter 2 ladder: `public servant within section 21`.)
    `legally bound as such public servant not to engage in trade`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 168: Was the accused, as a public servant, legally bound not to engage in trade?
    `engages in trade`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 168: Did the accused engage in trade?
    `legally bound as such public servant not to purchase or bid for certain property`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 169: Was the accused, as a public servant, legally bound not to purchase or bid for certain property?
    `purchases or bids for that property`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 169: Did the accused purchase or bid for that property - in the accused's own name or another's, or jointly or in shares with others?
    `the property is purchased`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc s 169: Was the property in fact purchased? (It is then confiscated - part of the punishment, not an element.)
    `the trade or property`
        IS A STRING @desc The trade, or the property, as it is to read in the charge
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 168
`punishment prescribed by s 168` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "168"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to one year, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 12
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

-- s 168 defines and punishes in one breath with no verb of its own; the offence
-- ladder is the defining predicate (so `definitionFns` is empty).
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 168 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant unlawfully engaging in trade)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Trading Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 168` f IF
        "Whoever, being a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `legally bound as such public servant not to engage in trade`
    AND f's `engages in trade`

@export Frame a charge under section 168 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant unlawfully engaging in trade), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Trading Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 168` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "168" "public servant unlawfully engaging in trade"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 168`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 168` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant legally bound as such not to engage in trade, did engage in trade, namely ", f's `the trade or property`, `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "being a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound as such public servant not to engage in trade`) "legally bound as such not to engage in trade"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `engages in trade`) "engages in trade")))

§§ `s 169 - Public servant unlawfully buying or bidding for property`

--   169. Whoever, being a public servant, and being legally bound as such public
--   servant not to purchase or bid for certain property, purchases or bids for
--   that property, either in his own name or in the name of another, or jointly
--   or in shares with others, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term
--   which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both; and the property,
--   if purchased, shall be confiscated.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 169
`punishment prescribed by s 169` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "169"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both; and the property, if purchased, shall be confiscated"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `shall be punished with`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

-- FORK SP-169: "the property, if purchased, shall be confiscated" is recorded as
-- forfeiture `shall be punished with`; the record cannot say "if purchased", the words do.
@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 169 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant unlawfully buying or bidding for property)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Trading Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 169` f IF
        "Whoever, being a"
    AND f's `public servant`
    AND f's `legally bound as such public servant not to purchase or bid for certain property`
    AND f's `purchases or bids for that property`

@export Frame a charge under section 169 of the Penal Code 1871 (public servant unlawfully buying or bidding for property), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Trading Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 169` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "169" "public servant unlawfully buying or bidding for property"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 169`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 169` f)
        (CONCAT "being a public servant legally bound as such not to purchase or bid for certain property, did ", (IF f's `the property is purchased` THEN "purchase" ELSE "bid for"), " that property, namely ", f's `the trade or property`, `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `public servant`) "being a public servant"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `legally bound as such public servant not to purchase or bid for certain property`) "legally bound as such not to purchase or bid for certain property"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `purchases or bids for that property`) "purchases or bids for that property")))

§§ `s 170 - Personating a public servant`

--   170. Whoever pretends to hold any particular office as a public servant,
--   knowing that he does not hold such office, or falsely personates any other
--   person holding such office, and in such assumed character does or attempts
--   to do any act under colour of such office, shall be punished with
--   imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with
--   both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 170
DECLARE `Personation of Public Servant Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `pretends to hold any particular office as a public servant`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused pretend to hold a particular office as a public servant (for example, a police officer)?
    `knowing that he does not hold such office`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know they did not hold that office?
    `falsely personates any other person holding such office`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused falsely personate another person who holds such an office?
    `in such assumed character`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what the accused did done in that assumed character?
    `does or attempts to do any act under colour of such office`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused do, or attempt to do, an act under colour of that office?
    `the office`
        IS A STRING @desc The office pretended, as it is to read in the charge - for example "a police officer"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 170
`punishment prescribed by s 170` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "170"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 2 years, or with fine, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 24
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS NOTHING
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused pretends to hold, or personates the holder of, a public office and acts under colour of it, within section 170 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Personation of Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `personates a public servant` f IF
        "Whoever"
    AND (    (    f's `pretends to hold any particular office as a public servant`
              AND f's `knowing that he does not hold such office` )
         OR  f's `falsely personates any other person holding such office` )
    AND "and"
    AND f's `in such assumed character`
    AND f's `does or attempts to do any act under colour of such office`

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 170 of the Penal Code 1871 (personating a public servant)
GIVEN f IS A `Personation of Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 170` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `personates a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 170 of the Penal Code 1871 (personating a public servant), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Personation of Public Servant Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 170` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "170" "personating a public servant"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 170`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 170` f)
        (CONCAT (IF f's `falsely personates any other person holding such office` THEN CONCAT "did falsely personate a person holding the office of ", f's `the office` ELSE CONCAT "did pretend to hold the office of ", f's `the office`, ", a public servant, knowing that you did not hold such office"), ", and in such assumed character did an act under colour of such office", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` ((f's `pretends to hold any particular office as a public servant` AND f's `knowing that he does not hold such office`) OR f's `falsely personates any other person holding such office`) "pretends to hold a particular office as a public servant, knowing he does not hold it, or falsely personates a person holding it"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `in such assumed character`) "in such assumed character"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `does or attempts to do any act under colour of such office`) "does or attempts to do any act under colour of such office"),
            (`missing unless` (`personates a public servant` f) "the elements of section 170 taken together")))

§§ `s 171 - Wearing garb or carrying token used by public servant, with fraudulent intent`

--   171. Whoever, not belonging to a certain class of public servants, wears any
--   garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by that class of
--   public servants, with the intention that it may be believed, or with the
--   knowledge that it is likely to be believed, that he belongs to that class of
--   public servants, shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may
--   extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $1,000, or with both.

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 171
DECLARE `Public Servant Garb Facts` HAS
    particulars
        IS A Particulars @desc Who is charged, and when and where the offence was committed
    `not belonging to a certain class of public servants`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the accused NOT a member of the class of public servants whose garb or token it is?
    `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by that class of public servants`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused wear a garb, or carry a token, resembling one used by that class (for example, a police uniform or warrant card)?
    `with the intention that it may be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend it to be believed that they belonged to that class?
    `with the knowledge that it is likely to be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants`
        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused know it was likely to be believed that they belonged to that class?
    `the class`
        IS A STRING @desc The class of public servants, as it is to read in the charge - for example "police officers"
    `the garb or token`
        IS A STRING @desc The garb or token, as it is to read in the charge - for example "a police uniform"
    `to wit`
        IS A STRING @desc How the accused did it, as it is to read after "to wit," at the end of the charge - for example "by refusing to alight from the vehicle when directed to do so"; leave blank if not needed

@ref Penal Code 1871 s 171
`punishment prescribed by s 171` MEANS Punishment WITH
    section                  IS "171"
    words                    IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 6 months, or with fine which may extend to $1,000, or with both"
    death                    IS `not prescribed`
    `imprisonment for life`  IS `not prescribed`
    imprisonment             IS `or with`
    `maximum term in months` IS JUST 6
    `minimum term in months` IS NOTHING
    `forfeiture of property` IS `not prescribed`
    fine                     IS `or with`
    `maximum fine`           IS JUST 1000
    `minimum fine`           IS NOTHING
    caning                   IS `not prescribed`
    `minimum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `maximum strokes`        IS NOTHING
    `or with both`           IS TRUE

@export Whether the accused, not belonging to a class of public servants, wears its garb or carries its token intending or knowing it likely to be believed that the accused belongs to it, within section 171 of the Penal Code 1871
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Garb Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wears the garb of a public servant` f IF
        "Whoever,"
    AND f's `not belonging to a certain class of public servants`
    AND f's `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by that class of public servants`
    AND (    f's `with the intention that it may be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants`
         OR  f's `with the knowledge that it is likely to be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants` )

@export Whether the accused has committed an offence punishable under section 171 of the Penal Code 1871 (wearing the garb or carrying the token of a public servant with fraudulent intent)
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Garb Facts` @desc The facts of the case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `offence under s 171` f IF
        "Whoever"
    ... `wears the garb of a public servant` f

@export Frame a charge under section 171 of the Penal Code 1871 (wearing the garb or carrying the token of a public servant with fraudulent intent), or say why none can be framed
GIVEN f IS A `Public Servant Garb Facts` @desc The facts of the case, and the particulars of the charge
GIVETH A Charge
`charge under s 171` f MEANS
    `frame the charge` (f's particulars) "171" "wearing the garb or carrying the token of a public servant with fraudulent intent"
        ((`punishment prescribed by s 171`)'s words)
        (`offence under s 171` f)
        (CONCAT "not belonging to the class of public servants, namely ", f's `the class`, ", did wear or carry ", f's `the garb or token`, ", resembling a garb or token used by that class, ", (IF f's `with the intention that it may be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants` THEN "with the intention that it might be believed" ELSE "with the knowledge that it was likely to be believed"), " that you belonged to that class of public servants", `the to-wit clause` (f's `to wit`))
        (concat (LIST
            (`missing unless` (f's `not belonging to a certain class of public servants`) "not belonging to a certain class of public servants"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `wears any garb or carries any token resembling any garb or token used by that class of public servants`) "wears a garb or carries a token resembling one used by that class"),
            (`missing unless` (f's `with the intention that it may be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants` OR f's `with the knowledge that it is likely to be believed that he belongs to that class of public servants`) "with the intention, or knowledge of the likelihood, that it be believed he belongs to that class"),
            (`missing unless` (`wears the garb of a public servant` f) "the elements of section 171 taken together")))
